====Usage notes====
The English word ''pronoun'' is used with a different meaning than ''Pronomen''. "[[ours]]" is a possessive pronoun, but "[[our]]" is a possessive adjective. In German, however, both kinds of words are called ''Pronomen''. The grammatical difference can be expressed by calling "ours" a ''substantivisches Pronomen'' and "our" an ''adjektivisches Pronomen''.

